flowchart TB
    accTitle: Proposal within the CoALA decision cycle
    accDescr: Current working information enters planning. Proposal generates candidates. Later planning responsibilities and execution are shown only as context and are not explained in this chapter.

    WM[Current working information] --> PLAN[Planning stage]
    PLAN --> PROP[Proposal: generate candidate actions]
    PROP --> CAND[One or more candidates]
    CAND --> LATER[Later planning work: evaluation and selection]
    LATER --> EXEC[Execution of the selected action]
    EXEC --> OUT[External interaction or internal learning]
    OUT --> FEEDBACK[Observation may become available]
    FEEDBACK -.-> WM

    NOTE[Chapter 6 focuses on proposal only]
    NOTE -.-> PROP

    classDef focus fill:#EAF4FB,stroke:#1A4A8A,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:2px;
    classDef context fill:#F4F4F4,stroke:#888888,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.2px;
    classDef store fill:#EEF7EE,stroke:#27AE60,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.2px;
    class PROP focus;
    class PLAN,CAND,LATER,EXEC,OUT,NOTE context;
    class WM,FEEDBACK store;
